<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yazdegerd II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 438–457</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yazdegerd II was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> from 438 to 457. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> briefly and campaigned for years against the Kidarites and other Hunnic peoples on his north-eastern frontier. His attempt to impose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zoroastrianism">Zoroastrianism</a> on the Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenians">Armenians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberians">Iberians</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> provoked the rising crushed at Avarayr in 451.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yazdegerd-ii.jpg" alt="Yazdegerd II" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:YazdegerdIICroppedCoinHistoryofIran.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
